    "section_faq_kxCLpz": {
      "type": "section-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "text_CBMiJt": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Production Seamstress/Seamster | Part-time and Full-time available",
            "content": "<ul><li>$19-$22/hr DOE</li><li>Flexible Schedule</li><li>On-site gym and game room</li><li>Unlimited use of public transit with ORCA card</li></ul><p>In this important role, you will be responsible for every step of the custom and semi-custom garment making process, including cutting, sewing, and finishing. All work will be performed at our facility - <strong>this is not a take-home role</strong>.<br/><br/>Our ideal candidate will possess:<br/>-At least one year of commercial production/piecework sewing experience.<br/>-Sample-making experience.<br/>-Ability to work quickly while maintaining high quality standards.<br/><br/>Job requirements include:<br/>-Basic English proficiency and ability to follow instructions.<br/>-Experience and familiarity with a variety of sewing machines and equipment.<br/>-Ability to work well in a small team environment.<br/>-Ability to work with minimal supervision.<br/>-Ability to lift a 40lb box to shoulder level.<br/><br/>If you have the skill, experience and interest, come join our friendly team!<br/><br/>Interested candidates, please reply with a basic resume describing relevant work experience.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_fdNJj6": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Fulfillment Processing Associate",
            "content": "<p><strong>Job description for Processing Associate:</strong></p><p>Voyagers K9 Apparel is a family-owned small business that has been making dog apparel for nearly 30 years. We pride ourselves on making high-quality, performance outerwear that keeps active dogs comfy in all weather environments. Our products are enjoyed by customers around the world. We are located in a clean and spacious facility in downtown Tacoma, just steps from the light rail and public transit station, and easy access to parking.</p><p><br/></p><p>We have a current opening for a Fulfillment Processing Associate. This important role is primarily responsible for helping us keep our promise to deliver a quality product in a timely manner to our customers. To accomplish this, the Fulfillment Processing Associate will ensure daily orders are pulled, checked for accuracy, packed and shipped.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>Key Responsibilities: </strong></p><ul><li>Picking and packing incoming orders</li><li>Adhering to fulfillment process guidelines</li><li>Maintaining production queue</li><li>Inventory management</li><li>Perform Quality Assurance (QA) inspections</li></ul><p><strong>Required skills and abilities:</strong></p><ul><li>Excellent attention to detail</li><li>Identify and match patterns in SKU codes</li><li>Lift 40lbs above shoulder height</li><li>Prioritize and complete tasks</li><li>Work quickly and efficiently with minimal supervision</li></ul><p><strong>Qualifications:</strong></p><ul><li>Eligible to work in the United States</li><li>English language fluency, spoken and written</li></ul><p><strong>Benefits include:</strong></p><ul><li>ORCA card</li><li>On site fitness facility</li><li>Flexible working hours</li><li>Paid sick leave</li></ul><p>This is an ideal role for a student. This is a seasonal position with flexible hours. Regular business hours are 7:30am to 4:30pm, Monday through Friday excluding holidays. After a probationary period, this role is eligible to work an alternative schedule, including evenings and weekends.</p>"
          }
        },
